{"name": "n1_unification", "sha256": "7a6c8424d0de47f18e65a81910d114f65c2ea42e7e8b2475ae9a913702b20f39", "words": 57, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.8841311940265195e-15, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:30Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 60, 0, 332, "When I say “unification”, I mean whatever pulls everything together so that a person can talk, cross a road, recognize a friend and answer a text, and it works even when there’s no separate knower in there. Most of my daily life includes that ordinary unification and feels almost like everybody else’s day (well, if they’re happy)."]]}
{"name": "n1_nde", "sha256": "7a28c5435e930d57d8f199a7f3108aa22bf0835e55f1cb711040b854bf4f84cc", "words": 108, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 8.039063630457175e-32, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:32Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 122, 0, 690, "The closest comparison that’s worth mentioning is the out-of-body perception in some near-death experiences. People sometimes report seeing things from impossible angles, and a controversial subset of those reports were verified by others in the room. Those cases had a target that other people could check, and my room experience didn’t, since I wasn’t floating around noticing specific details. So they can’t vouch for my event, but they help show what I mean by an experience that wasn’t stuck at the body’s vantage point anymore. If you want to dig in, there’s this systematic analysis of near-death reports, the AWARE-II cardiac-arrest study, and a recent veridical-NDE evidence scale."]]}
{"name": "n1_percentages", "sha256": "047a345f3eed238f4d84c61907999417d7b86fa71fc0b1bac176d6e980ffb447", "words": 96, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.5092214941978455, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.32279298762206e-13, "fraction_human": 0.49077847599983215, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:33Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 44, 0, 288, "This distinction isn’t laid out explicitly in the suttas. AN 11.12 says a noble disciple can reach ease and joy through recollecting the Buddha, Dhamma, & Saṅgha – the community of realized disciples – or recollecting ethical conduct, generosity, or qualities shared with heavenly beings."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 11, 288, 358, " In my experience there can also be physical loosening of unification."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 41, 358, 587, " My percentages are just playful shorthand for how much binding has dissolved, and partial untying isn’t limited to the range I give: at around 1% a person can still do everything fine, and by roughly 5% they can barely function."]]}
{"name": "n1_burden", "sha256": "ef1e3473b482adbf978c74ec672b1a7cb036b65dfb6c9f4635aac14dbb7fc98e", "words": 78, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.9999998211860657, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.7059811679639991e-12, "fraction_human": 1.854610616192076e-07, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:35Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 72, 0, 389, "In SN 22.22 the Buddha keeps two things apart: the five aggregates are the burden, and craving is what picks it up. The tangle is heavy all by itself (even an arahant still feels the first dart), and craving is why we keep carrying it. Physics actually agrees that binding is heavy, literally: quarks supply less than 1% of a proton’s mass, and roughly 99% comes from gluon-binding energy."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 6, 389, 428, " Matter weighs what its binding weighs."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 3, 428, 450, " Light weighs nothing."]]}
{"name": "n1_last_test", "sha256": "61375c501e172c3a64ea3b132365d208e55dfd497e072e41de93e2509612bc5c", "words": 47, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 2.4125602557378834e-11, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.604103615949836e-26, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:37Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 0, 57, "Can you still recognize trauma without floating above it?"], ["Human Written", "High", 41, 57, 276, "\nI’m asking that last one because a stream-enterer still has most of the fetters. They still need to do reparenting like other folks, and even a real breakthrough won’t turn somebody into a therapist, let alone a saint."]]}
{"name": "n1_rebirth", "sha256": "c86c1b387e0344ed95cfabd70fe16b0a996f7f34766c961ce8ced05ad0715491", "words": 96, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 0.0005874581984244287, "fraction_ai_assisted": 4.3065189855708274e-29, "fraction_human": 0.9994125366210938, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:38Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 45, 0, 253, "Stream entry’s greatest prize is a “release date”: AN 3.88  allows at most seven more lives before final awakening. There is actually quite a lot of modern academic evidence for rebirth. But who’s going around getting reborn if no permanent self exists?"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 253, 332, " Buddhists don’t imagine any permanent self-essence/soul moving between bodies."], ["Human Written", "Low", 31, 332, 524, " What continues is a chain of causes with no traveler riding along, often called a mind-stream: craving and clinging condition becoming, and becoming becomes birth. More like a driverless car."], ["Human Written", "High", 15, 524, 629, " The later Buddhist philosopher Milindapañha compared rebirth to one lamp being used to lighting another."]]}
{"name": "n1_diamond", "sha256": "62054d8c775a78cb3bcd210e2d79c87e67bfbf69196661507897362723c4ebcc", "words": 82, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 5.948632721541998e-22, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:40Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 83, 0, 443, "I used to attribute “life is like a dream” directly to the historical Buddha. Turns out the famous stanza I loved comes from the later Mahāyāna Diamond Sutra, which puts some words in his mouth. The early Pāli texts do have images that are pretty close, though: SN 22.95 compares form to foam, feeling to a bubble, perception to a mirage and consciousness to a magic trick, and Dhammapada 170 asks us to see the world as a bubble and a mirage."]]}
{"name": "n1_science", "sha256": "b9501c01973e01a6a5469cd3038df3e8acb6eaffc22637ff81e7674238122371", "words": 93, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 2.414550726825837e-05, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.3085142156323577e-13, "fraction_human": 0.999975860118866, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:41Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Low", 94, 0, 567, "Science only gets to circle the edges of consciousness, though it finds some wild stuff out there: people functioning with no felt controller, several things cognized at once, split-brain patients who can seem like two knowers sharing a skull, and one recent theory that models minds as nested parallel observers. The full nerdy tour is in the research report. Science gives my argument a third wheel, making it safer to ride, but it will never show nibbāna itself – self and sense organs unweaving into self-presenting light flows of bliss. That requires meditation."]]}
{"name": "n1_driving", "sha256": "1388441818f24f3f14c33265ae45698ac630a84f10225f35bedcbda7a67a405d", "words": 92, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8041679263114929, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.19579295814037323, "fraction_human": 3.9140020817285404e-05, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:24:42Z", "windows": [["AI-Assisted", "Low", 24, 0, 133, "My buddy E. told me he had much stronger episodes while driving: for long stretches, his own car and the traffic seemed to disappear."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 6, 133, 166, " He never had an accident either."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 60, 166, 498, " Maybe he was just lucky, or he misunderstood what was happening, or there’s something about how these states work, or some mix of those, or God only knows.\nEither way, I wouldn’t keep driving through that myself. If you’re having episodes like that, I’d stay away from driving or running machinery until you understand them better."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 6, 498, 527, " That’s my own CYA showing. 😇"]]}
